    "sections": {
        "description": "<h4>GDPR</h4>\n<p>According to the GDPR, the user must actively agree if content is to be loaded from third-party servers.</p>\n<p>The WordPress plugins</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Leaflet Map</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/extensions-leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Extensions for Leaflet Map</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/wp-gpx-maps/\" rel=\"ugc\">WP GPX Maps</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>are loading content from the defined tile servers and may be from other servers too.</p>\n<p>This plugin requests the user&#8217;s permission to load the maps.<br />\nYou can customize the text and use it on your own responsibility.</p>\n<p>The plugin does work with <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/cartoblocks-for-leaflet/\" rel=\"ugc\">CartoBlocks for Leaflet</a> and supports <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/theme-translation-for-polylang/\" rel=\"ugc\">Theme and plugin translation for Polylang (TTfP)</a>.</p>\n<h4>Documentation</h4>\n<p>Documentation in <a href=\"https://leafext.de/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">German</a>, <a href=\"https://leafext.de/en/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">English</a> and an <a href=\"https://leafext.de/extra/dsgvo-example/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">example</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ul>\n<li>Install and configure Leaflet Map or WP GPX Maps.</li>\n<li>Then install this plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to the Settings and get documentation and settings options.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "faq": "\n<h4>\nIs that enough to comply with the GDPR?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ul>\n<li>I don&#8217;t know, ask a law expert.</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n<h4>\nHow can I report security bugs?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can report security bugs through the Patchstack Vulnerability Disclosure Program. The Patchstack team help validate, triage and handle any security vulnerabilities. <a href=\"https://patchstack.com/database/vdp/5160a9e7-37f1-4a28-9c83-2adf50991e2f\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Report a security vulnerability.</a></li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h3>261107 / Version 4.1</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for WP GPX Maps</li>\n<li>Support for CartoBlocks for Leaflet</li>\n<li>new Description</li>\n</ul>\n<p>see <a href=\"https://github.com/hupe13/dsgvo-leaflet-map-github/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Changelog</a></p>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Respect the DSGVO / GDPR when you use Leaflet Map or WP GPX Maps.",
    "description": "<h4>GDPR</h4>\n<p>According to the GDPR, the user must actively agree if content is to be loaded from third-party servers.</p>\n<p>The WordPress plugins</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Leaflet Map</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/extensions-leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Extensions for Leaflet Map</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/wp-gpx-maps/\" rel=\"ugc\">WP GPX Maps</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>are loading content from the defined tile servers and may be from other servers too.</p>\n<p>This plugin requests the user&#8217;s permission to load the maps.<br />\nYou can customize the text and use it on your own responsibility.</p>\n<p>The plugin does work with <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/cartoblocks-for-leaflet/\" rel=\"ugc\">CartoBlocks for Leaflet</a> and supports <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/theme-translation-for-polylang/\" rel=\"ugc\">Theme and plugin translation for Polylang (TTfP)</a>.</p>\n<h4>Documentation</h4>\n<p>Documentation in <a href=\"https://leafext.de/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">German</a>, <a href=\"https://leafext.de/en/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">English</a> and an <a href=\"https://leafext.de/extra/dsgvo-example/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">example</a>.</p>\n",
